 "version": 1,
 "blurb": "Turns the shot into old paint on a wall and lets it peel. As Peel goes up, hairline cracks open across the picture, the paint lifts from the cracks inwards and curls up into lips that catch the light, show their chalky underside and throw shadows, and the oldest flakes fall away to bare plaster, concrete, wood or an older coat of paint underneath. Peeling starts in patches, the way a real wall goes. Key Peel, or set Peels over to watch it happen.",
